{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Observe the month of the spring</b> — it explains the commandment of the festivals, for it has already been mentioned (Leviticus 23; Numbers 28–29). Now, in Torat Kohanim he mentioned the matter of the sacrifices — 'and you shall bring a fire-offering to YHWH' — whereas here he does not mention them at all; rather, he warns Israel to go up with them to the place that He will choose and to rejoice before Him. For just as He commanded that one bring second tithe before HaShem, and likewise the firstborn, and eat them there at the place that HaShem will choose, so He added to explain that they are further obligated that they all come before HaShem and celebrate before Him on the three pilgrimage festivals, and rejoice with the peace-offerings that they bring before Him. And he did not mention the times of the Festival of Unleavened Bread and of Booths — on which day they shall fall — but rather mentioned their months in brief, for he had already mentioned everything there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:22.269157814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}